# Curated artefact -- Phase 4, QHV twin leg, an INVALID test kept for the record (2026-09-08).
# QEMU 6.2.0 with "-device virtio-rng-device" added directly after virtio-blk (slot 2), no net.
# It was read at the time as "entropy starvation ruled out". It ruled out nothing: the image
# probes the rng at virtio-mmio slot 3 (random ... devr-virtio.so:mem=0xa003a00), and this log
# still contains "random: Unable to use devr-virtio.so as an entropy source" -- QNX never saw
# the device. The 419-byte length equals the blk-only hang exactly. See the q62-rng log for the
# corrected test (rng in slot 3), and docs/findings.md 2026-07-28 for why slot order matters.
# QEMU args (identical to scripts/launch-qhv-tcg.ps1 / scripts/orin/launch-qhv-on-orin-tcg.sh
# at the time): -machine virt,virtualization=on,gic-version=3 -cpu max -accel tcg -smp 2 -m 2G
#   -drive file=disk-qemu,if=none,id=drv0,format=raw -device virtio-blk-device,drive=drv0
#   [-netdev user,id=n0 -device virtio-net-device,netdev=n0 -object rng-builtin,id=rng0
#    -device virtio-rng-device,rng=rng0]   <- only where the header says rng=slot3
#   -kernel ifs.bin -serial file:<log> -display none -no-reboot
# Images: ifs.bin b2d875057f25a4cbda69966e553629d445cfa44af62cf4c5e121442c9782300a,
#         disk-qemu c71b9499353ca4b1d2c4bffbdebbc509bb12492d86cfb6e07e22d79451b7cdfe
#         (SHA-256 at copy time, verified on the Orin with sha256sum -c; NOTE the raw disk
#          mutates on every boot without -snapshot, which these runs did not use).
# Host: Jetson Orin Nano, L4T 5.15.148-tegra, Cortex-A78AE (CPU part 0xd42), 6 cores, 8 GB.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

